course: dictionary
lesson: 11740
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 1
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Bachelor is one of them. The words around it, its context, tell you which meaning is right.
explain: «My uncle Tom is a bachelor. He has never married and lives alone with his dog.» Here the clues are never married and lives alone, so a bachelor is a man who is not married and never has been.
explain: «Anna finished her bachelor's degree in science last summer.» Now the clues are degree and science. A bachelor's degree is a first university qualification, so this meaning has nothing to do with a man.
fact: A bachelor is a man who is not married and never has been.
fact: A bachelor's degree is a first university degree, such as a Bachelor of Arts (BA) or a Bachelor of Science (BSc).
fact: Informally, a bachelor pad is a flat where an unmarried man lives.
fact: A confirmed bachelor is a man who has decided he will never marry.
fact: To choose the right meaning, look at the clues: a person means meaning one, and university means meaning two.
exercise: «My uncle is a bachelor and has never married.» What is a bachelor here? | A married man with three children | A teacher at a school | *A man who has never married | A type of university building
exercise: «Mia finished her bachelor's degree in music.» What does bachelor's degree mean? | A small flat with one room | A man who is not married | A card for a birthday party | *A first university degree
exercise: The flat has one chair, a pizza box, and no curtains. Dan calls it a bachelor pad. What does bachelor pad mean? | A hall where people get married | A classroom at school | A large house for a whole family | *A flat where an unmarried man lives
test: «Grandpa was a bachelor all his life.» Which clue helps you most to find the meaning? | *all his life, so he never married | a | Grandpa | was
test: «Ben studied for a Bachelor of Science at college.» What does bachelor mean here? | A bachelor pad | *A first university degree | A man who is not married | A kind of college teacher
exam: Which sentence uses bachelor to mean a man who is not married? | *«Our neighbour is a bachelor, and he has never married.» | «We stayed in a bachelor flat with one bedroom.» | «Ella's bachelor's degree took three years.»
